[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629044561","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100056#issuecomment-2629044561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100056","id":2629044561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ctAlR","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T17:47:51Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T22:56:29Z","body":"I don't have time to do a very deep dive on this, but note that this PR breaks with any sort of movement during idle processing when the physics tick rate is lower than the idle tick rate, where the transformations seem to compound in some way.\r\n\r\nThe simplest way to repro is to just set `physics/common/physics_ticks_per_second` to `30`, and apply the following script to an `AnimatableBody3D`:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends AnimatableBody3D\r\n\r\nvar elapsed := 0.0\r\n\r\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\r\n\telapsed += delta\r\n\tglobal_position.x = sin(elapsed)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlternatively you can also animate it using an `AnimationPlayer` node, with a `position` track, while leaving the `AnimationPlayer`'s `callback_mode_process` property at the default of `ANIMATION_CALLBACK_MODE_PROCESS_IDLE`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629044561/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629592596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100056#issuecomment-2629592596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100056","id":2629592596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cvGYU","user":{"login":"huwpascoe","id":1812087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTIwODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1812087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe","html_url":"https://github.com/huwpascoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T22:41:47Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T22:41:47Z","body":"Found out my test model was just wrong. And can't figure out the correct sequence of matrix transforms to make this work, sorry.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629592596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630598220","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100056#issuecomment-2630598220","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100056","id":2630598220,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cy75M","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T10:51:05Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T10:51:05Z","body":"I guess the problem is that you can't really distinguish between a relative transformation (`position.x += delta`) and an absolute transformation (`position.x = sin(elapsed)`) with the revert approach used by `sync_to_physics`, so you're forced to assume one or the other.\r\n\r\nIn fact, the code currently seems to assume only absolute transformations, so you'll find that `position.x += delta` is currently broken when done from the idle processing, whereas I guess your PR would have fixed this but instead breaks absolute transformations.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630598220/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]